  (text "AUDIO OUT (authentic Model 1 sound, no clean mode). Everything here runs on the quiet +4V5A rail around VREF = 2.25V.\n1. 2.2k load on MOL / MOR, as in the Mega Amp, so the chip's DAC works as it did in the console.\n2. Model 1 style low-pass: inverting OPA2350 stage, 47k in, 100k || 470pF feedback. First order, 3.39 kHz, gain about 2.1.\n   That matches the 47k / 1nF Model 1 filter used by MIDIbox. Change C to 560pF for 2.84 kHz (the VA3 knee) after the A/B test in M4.\n3. Balanced line outs: cold = filter out, hot = filter out inverted again by a 10k / 10k OPA2350 stage. 100 ohm + 10uF + 100k bleed\n   on each leg into a Neutrik 1/4in TRS (tip hot, ring cold, sleeve to GND through a 0 ohm ground-lift footprint).\n4. Headphones: 10uF DC block, dual slide pot on its 6-pin plug (volume, headphones only), 1uF into a TPA6132A2 at -6 dB gain.\n   Its outputs are ground-centred, so they go straight to the front 3.5 mm jack. GP12 (HP_EN) mutes it until the rail settles." (at 25.4 20.32 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9a10b5d4-5570-5174-be96-7d0e0f48cbbc)
  )
)
